ok - orders append as single JSON lines with ids that rise by one
ok - waiters racing to reclaim a dead owner's lock never duplicate an order id
ok - a signalled append exits without writing and without deleting another writer's lock
ok - a poll signalled while it holds the ledger lock exits and releases it
ok - delivery repeats until every order is acked, never stacks, and keeps no state besides the ledger
ok - an order never queued is queued even when another producer advanced the wake sequence
ok - pending fails rather than printing a partial list when the ledger cannot be read
ok - a ledger or acks path that is not a regular file is refused instead of re-listing every order
ok - a malformed ledger or acks file exits non-zero naming the file, never success with no orders
ok - an append that cannot be published leaves the ledger as it was
ok - ack refuses ids too large for bash arithmetic and never acks a different order
ok - a real wake-queue write failure fails the poll and the order is announced on a later one
ok - an append that cannot take the lock refuses and names the owner
ok - racing polls queue exactly one wake
ok - a poll that cannot read the ledger keeps the last good pending view
ok - a replay with the doorbell off is acked on both secondmate homes in 7s
ok - concurrent appends take distinct monotonic ids
ok - an ack removes exactly the acked id from pending, in any order
ok - acking an id with no order line is refused and changes nothing
ok - a poll shows pending orders and queues one wake each without any doorbell
ok - an order is never lost or silenced when one poll cannot announce it
